Typical Instruments: Vast synthesized orchestral arrays (modeled on rare 21st-century VSTs), Game Boy/NES sound chips meticulously circuit-bent and granularized, analog modular synthesizers generating deep, liquid tech-house basslines and percussive glitches, and meticulously close-miked and digitally processed tabla drums. New invented instruments include the 'Cryo-Harmonica,' a glass sculpture played by freezing and thawing it, and the 'Data-Stream Weaver,' a custom-built controller that lets performers physically manipulate sound via real-time data input from climate sensors.

